 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0 (2025-10-20)
+
+- Ticket assignment: `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to an agent, or unassigns it
+  (`{"assignee": null}`). Every ticket includes `assignee` (null when unassigned). The assigned agent is notified.
+- `GET /tickets?assignee=` filters by agent; an empty value lists unassigned tickets. Combined filters all have to match.
+- The command-line listing shows each ticket's assignee.
+
+## 1.5.0 (2025-10-06)
+
+- Due times: each ticket is due a number of hours after it was created (4 urgent, 24 high, 72 normal, 168 low), stored
+  as `due` and listed by `GET /tickets?overdue=true` ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Hours are
+  `DUE_HOURS_*` and are not applied again to a ticket that already has `due`.
+- `DUE_TIMES=on` shows due times. Until then the API is unchanged. 1.4.0 still starts on a data file this release wrote.
+- `POST /tickets/import` creates many tickets in one request (at most 5000), all of them or none, for the move from the
+  old tracker. Each is recorded and its requester is notified as when one ticket is created.
+
 ## 1.4.0 (2025-09-15)
 
 - The operator command line, `bin/tickets.js` (`list`, `show`), and the weekly report, `scripts/weekly-report.js`.
